<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy"
	accent="Policy."
	description="This policy explains what Gatherory collects, why we use it, and the choices you have when you plan and share an event."
	updated="October 10, 2026"
	activePage="privacy"
>
	<ol slot="toc">
		<li><a href="#scope">Scope</a></li>
		<li><a href="#information">Information we collect</a></li>
		<li><a href="#use">How we use information</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sharing">How we share information</a></li>
		<li><a href="#cookies">Cookies and analytics</a></li>
		<li><a href="#retention">Retention and security</a></li>
		<li><a href="#choices">Your choices</a></li>
		<li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
		<li><a href="#international">International transfers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
	</ol>

	<div class="legal-callout">
		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<p>Gatherory uses your information to provide a shared place for planning events. Your event content is visible to the people you invite according to their role and the visibility you choose. We do not sell your personal information.</p>
	</div>

	<section id="scope">
		<h2>1. Scope</h2>
		<p>This Privacy Policy applies to Gatherory’s websites, applications, and related services. It does not cover third-party services that you choose to connect to or visit, which operate under their own privacy policies.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="information">
		<h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
		<p>We collect information you provide, information created as you use Gatherory, and limited technical information needed to operate and improve the service.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your name, email address, profile image, authentication details, account preferences, and workspace memberships. If you use Google or Apple to sign in, we receive the account details that provider makes available with your permission.</li>
			<li><strong>Event and planning content.</strong> Event names, dates, locations, schedules, ideas, decisions, notes, budgets, expenses, registry items, participant roles, attendance responses, and other details you add to a gathering.</li>
			<li><strong>Invitations and collaboration.</strong> Contact details used to invite someone, invitation status, and activity connected to hosts, collaborators, and guests.</li>
			<li><strong>Media.</strong> Images and related file information you upload for an event, idea, registry item, or invitation.</li>
			<li><strong>Communications.</strong> Messages you send to us, including support requests and feedback.</li>
			<li><strong>Usage and device information.</strong> Browser and device type, IP address, approximate location derived from an IP address, pages and features used, timestamps, diagnostic data, and similar log information.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Other people may provide information about you when they invite you to an event or add you as a participant. If you provide another person’s information, you are responsible for having permission to do so.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="use">
		<h2>3. How we use information</h2>
		<p>We use information to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>create and secure accounts, verify email addresses, and maintain sessions;</li>
			<li>provide event planning, invitations, collaboration, media, and attendance features;</li>
			<li>apply event roles and permissions so people see and change only the parts available to them;</li>
			<li>send transactional messages such as verification, password reset, sign-in, and invitation emails;</li>
			<li>respond to support requests and communicate about the service;</li>
			<li>monitor reliability, prevent abuse, troubleshoot problems, and improve Gatherory; and</li>
			<li>comply with law and protect the rights, safety, and integrity of Gatherory and its community.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="sharing">
		<h2>4. How we share information</h2>
		<p>Gatherory is collaborative by design. Event content and participant details are shared with hosts, collaborators, and guests according to the event role, access rules, and visibility settings selected by the people managing the event.</p>
		<p>We may also share information with:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Service providers.</strong> Companies that help us host the service, store data and private media, deliver email, provide authentication, monitor reliability, and understand product usage. They may process information only to perform services for us and under appropriate obligations.</li>
			<li><strong>Connected services.</strong> Google, Apple, or another service when you choose to connect it or use it to sign in.</li>
			<li><strong>Legal and safety recipients.</strong> Authorities or other parties when reasonably necessary to comply with law, respond to valid legal process, prevent fraud or abuse, or protect people and rights.</li>
			<li><strong>A successor.</strong> A buyer, investor, or successor in connection with a merger, financing, reorganization, or sale of all or part of the business, subject to appropriate confidentiality protections.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We may share aggregated or de-identified information that does not reasonably identify you. We do not sell your personal information.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="cookies">
		<h2>5. Cookies and analytics</h2>
		<p>Gatherory uses cookies and similar storage technologies to keep you signed in, remember preferences, protect accounts, and operate the service. When analytics is enabled, we may also use these technologies to understand which pages and features are used and to improve the experience.</p>
		<p>You can control cookies through your browser settings. Blocking required cookies may prevent sign-in or other parts of Gatherory from working correctly.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="retention">
		<h2>6. Retention and security</h2>
		<p>We keep personal information for as long as needed to provide Gatherory, maintain legitimate business records, resolve disputes, enforce agreements, and meet legal obligations. Retention can vary by the type of information and why it was collected. Event content may remain available to other authorized participants even after one participant leaves an event.</p>
		<p>We use administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect information. Private event media is stored with restricted access and is delivered through time-limited access methods. No system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="choices">
		<h2>7. Your choices</h2>
		<p>You can update certain account and event information in Gatherory, leave events when the product allows it, and manage browser cookies through your device settings. You may also ask us to access, correct, export, or delete personal information, or object to certain uses, where applicable law provides those rights.</p>
		<p>Some information may need to be retained for security, fraud prevention, legal compliance, or to preserve records shared with other event participants. To make a privacy request, contact us using the address below. We may need to verify your identity before completing it.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="children">
		<h2>8. Children</h2>
		<p>Gatherory is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information in violation of this policy, please contact us so we can review and take appropriate action.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="international">
		<h2>9. International transfers</h2>
		<p>Gatherory and its service providers may process information in countries other than the country where you live. Those countries may have different data-protection laws. Where required, we use appropriate safeguards for these transfers.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="changes">
		<h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
		<p>We may update this policy as Gatherory changes. If an update materially affects how we use personal information, we will provide notice through the service or another appropriate channel. The date at the top shows when this policy was last revised.</p>
		<p>Questions or privacy requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:privacy@gatherory.com">privacy@gatherory.com</a>.</p>
	</section>
</LegalLayout>
